{
  "_note": [
    "A PER-FILE floor, so the 95% aggregate cannot be met by trading a file away.",
    "Consumed by $GOH_DIR/gates/coverage_gate.sh --lang rust --floors-json, wired in .gatesrc.",
    "Seeded 2026-10-05 from the gate's own report: 96.79% of coverable lines, 16272/16811,",
    "126 source files under rust/src, 37 of them below 100%. file_floor is set a whole",
    "point BELOW the lowest measured non-exempt file (rust/src/cli_ztools_twitter.rs at",
    "73/98 = 74.4898%), never at or above it: the merger compares 100*cov/tot against this",
    "number with no rounding, so a floor written from the 74.49 the report PRINTS would sit",
    "above the file it was measured from and go red on arrival.",
    "POLICY. Every measured file must hold at least file_floor. It is a FLOOR, not a per-file",
    "ratchet: the rust mode takes one uniform number (a per-target map is refused, exit 2), so",
    "a file may drift from 99% to 74.5% silently. Closing that needs per-file values upstream.",
    "EXEMPTION, exactly one file. rust/src/ztools/twitter/native.rs measures 8/293 = 2.7%: it is",
    "the camoufox collect and login driver, and testing it means launching a real browser",
    "against a live session, which no test here may do. The key is RELATIVE TO THE PROJECT THE",
    "MERGER RUNS IN, which is rust/ (the step's last argument), so it reads src/..., not",
    "rust/src/...: a key the merger cannot match is reported stale and fails the gate.",
    "rust/src/main.rs is not exempt: it measures 6/6.",
    "MECHANICS. tolerance is 0.0: the comparison is exact, and a tolerance would only hide a",
    "regression. No // comments: the merger reads this with json.load, and an unreadable floors",
    "file is refused (exit 2) since gates_of_heck 22c8d49 -- loud, but still red."
  ],
  "file_floor": 74.0,
  "tolerance": 0.0,
  "exempt": {
    "src/ztools/twitter/native.rs": "8/293 covered: the camoufox collect+login driver. Only a real browser against a live session exercises it, which no test in this repo may launch, so a floor here would be fiction."
  }
}
